    description: "Follow-up to INV-lukop (the minified-heuristic gate). When the default supply-chain tier filter drops a file classified tier-4 (DERIVED) — minified/bundled/generated web assets, and any future mis-tier — EVERY symbol and edge for that file vanishes from the behavior map with NO diagnostic (analysis_incomplete stays False, limits.failed_files stays []). INV-lukop fixed the specific dense-non-web-file misclassification; this item generalizes the honesty half: record tier-filtered file drops in limits (e.g. a limits.tier_filtered_files list or reuse supply_chain_summary.derived_skipped at file granularity) so a consumer can see WHAT was dropped and WHY, rather than silently receiving an incomplete graph. Assessment note: keep it to a recording line at the file-drop chokepoint — do NOT re-architect the tier filter. Locate the file-level DERIVED-drop site first (distinct from the cli.py --max-tier entrypoint/slice filters)."  # e79e
    fields: {}  # e79e
